# content-migration/ working data (docs/08-content-migration.md): raw HTML
# dumps, downloaded media, and the giant per-page extraction dump are scrape
# working files already condensed into cms-import.json (the file the real
# importer reads) and asset-manifest.json (source->local mapping). Keeping
# ~85MB of raw/rendered scrape output in git history forever isn't worth it;
# the smaller manifests/reports/cleaned-text stay tracked for auditability.
/content-migration/raw
/content-migration/assets
/content-migration/rendered-pages.json

